  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1,350 MW Abuja Project, through Continuum Associates, LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A grant to Nigeria National Petroleum Company (NNPC) Gas Power Investment Company Limited funds a feasibility study for 1,350 megawatt gas-fired project that will deliver power to Abuja through the national grid. The project will meet the goals of the Electrify Africa Act, the U.S. Government&apos;s Power Africa and Prosper Africa Initiatives, and U.S. Trade and Development Agency&apos;s (USTDA) U.S. Gas Infrastructure Exports Initiative and will support the goals of Nigeria&apos;s Power Sector Recovery Program and Economic Recovery and Growth Plan by supporting diversification of the country&apos;s energy industry. The Study will be undertaken on a sole source basis by the U.S. firm, Continuum Associates Limited Liability Corporation.</narrative>
  </description>
